frames/

# Keep output GIFs (negation rules)
!logo.gif
!icon.gif

# dot_swarm trail — remove to make visible (swarm trail visible).
# NOTE: `.swarm/*` (not `.swarm/`) is deliberate — git cannot re-include a
# path whose PARENT directory is itself excluded ("It is not possible to
# re-include a file if a parent directory of that file is excluded" — git
# docs), so a blanket `.swarm/` would silently defeat the negation below no
# matter how it's written. This is also why the 5 core .swarm/*.md files
# needed `git add -f` rather than a negation pattern.
.swarm/*

# SWC-048: per-agent PUBLIC keys are safe to commit and MUST be shared for
# signature verification to work across a fresh clone/new agent instance —
# un-ignore them specifically rather than force-adding one file at a time.
# Never un-ignore the private key itself — it never lives under .swarm/ at
# all (see identity.py), so there's nothing to accidentally commit here.
!.swarm/agents/
!.swarm/agents/*.json
